#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
template_extract.py

Dump every formatting decision baked into a .docx / .dotx so it can be turned
into a config file instead of Python code.

    python3 template_extract.py TEMPLATE.docx
    python3 template_extract.py TEMPLATE.docx -o dump --redact-body
    python3 template_extract.py TEMPLATE.docx --redact-all --no-media

Outputs into the output directory (default: <template stem>_dump/):

    report.md          human readable, read this first
    dump.json          full fidelity, machine readable
    xml/*.xml          pretty printed copies of the parts that matter
    media/*            every image in the file, extracted

Standard library only. No pip install, no network. Python 3.8+.
Reads the file. Never writes to it.

REDACTION
    (default)        everything, including body text
    --redact-body    keeps headings and style names, replaces other body text
                     with <len=NN>. Headers/footers are kept since that is
                     where letterhead and markings live.
    --redact-all     replaces every piece of text everywhere. Structure only.
"""

